# Changelog maintenance

After completing any task that changes product behaviour, add one line to the
**active changelog file** in the matching section.

## Active file

While repo root `version` is `X.Y.Z`, edit **only**:

```
changelog/changelog-v<NEXT>
```

where `<NEXT>` is the semver after one bump. So `version` = `1.0.0` means
you edit `changelog/changelog-v1.0.1`, never `-v1.0.0`. After `1.0.9`
the next file is `changelog-v1.1.0`, never `v1.0.10`.

### Mandatory pre-flight

1. Read repo root `version`. Never guess it from open tabs or recent files.
2. Resolve the path:

```powershell
. scripts/changelog-lib.ps1; Get-ActiveChangelogPath
```

3. Edit only that path.

## File layout

```
# vX.Y.Z

## Features
[feature] ...

## Improvements
[improvement] ...

## Bug fixes
[bugfix] ...
```

Types: `feature`, `bugfix`, `improvement`. English only.
